course: world
lesson: 115
title: What day of the week will it be?
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: The days of the week go round like the seats on a merry-go-round with 7 seats: every 7 days the same day comes back. So to find the day in 10 days' time, take out the whole weeks and count only what is left: 10 days is 1 week and 3 days, and Monday plus 3 days is Thursday.
explain: Dates that are 7 apart fall on the same weekday. If the 1st of a month is a Tuesday, so are the 8th, 15th, 22nd and 29th. Christmas Day and New Year's Day are exactly a week apart, so they always share a weekday: Christmas 2026 is on a Friday, and so is 1 January 2027.
explain: A normal year is 52 weeks and 1 day, so a date moves on one weekday each year; if a 29 February comes in between, it moves on two. A birthday on a Wednesday this year will be on a Thursday next year, and over the years it visits every day of the week.
explain: To find "the second Friday" or "the last Friday", find the first one and keep adding 7. Phones and computers use these same rules to find the weekday of any date, past or future, and the mathematician John Conway invented a trick, the "Doomsday rule", to do it in your head.
fact: Every 7 days the same weekday comes back, so to count on, take away whole weeks first and count the days left over.
fact: 10 days is 1 week and 3 days, so 10 days after a Monday is a Thursday.
fact: A normal year is 52 weeks and 1 day, so a date falls one weekday later the next year, or two weekdays later if a 29 February comes in between.
fact: Christmas Day and New Year's Day are 7 days apart, so they fall on the same weekday; in 2026 Christmas is on a Friday and 1 January 2027 is a Friday too.
fact: Halloween, 31 October 2026, is a Saturday, and Bonfire Night, 5 November, is 5 days later, on a Thursday.
fact: In Britain 5 November is Bonfire Night, remembering a plot in 1605 to blow up Parliament.
fact: If the 1st of a month is a Tuesday, the 8th, 15th, 22nd and 29th are Tuesdays too.
fact: "The second Friday" means the second time Friday comes in that month: if 1 June is a Monday, the first Friday is 5 June and the second is 12 June.
fact: A birthday moves round the days of the week, so it cannot fall on a Saturday every year.
fact: Every year has at least one Friday the 13th and at most three; in 2026 they are 13 February, 13 March and 13 November.
fact: The idea that Friday the 13th is unlucky is a superstition; nothing special really happens on those days.
fact: 1 January 2000 was a Saturday, and phones and computers use calendar rules to find the weekday of any date.
fact: In a 30-day month that starts on a Thursday, the Fridays are the 2nd, 9th, 16th, 23rd and 30th, so the last Friday is the 30th.
fact: Words people use: "no chance" means no way, "prepone" means move to an earlier time, the opposite of postpone (Indian English), "do the needful" means do what needs doing (Indian English) "y'all" means you all (southern USA), "no cap" means "no lie", "extra" means over the top, "it's giving" means "it seems like" and "you're having a laugh" means you must be joking (UK).
exercise: Today is Monday. Kai's party is in 10 days. What day is that? | Thursday | Wednesday | Friday | Monday
exercise: How many whole weeks and days are in 10 days? | 1 week and 3 days | 1 week and 4 days | 2 weeks and 3 days | 1 week and 1 day
exercise: Ella's birthday is on a Wednesday this year, and no 29 February comes before next year's. What day will it be next year? | Thursday | Wednesday | Friday | Tuesday
exercise: Why does a date move on one weekday each year? | A year is 52 weeks and 1 day | A year is exactly 52 weeks | A year is 50 weeks and 15 days | The week is 8 days long once a year
exercise: Christmas 2026 is on a Friday. What day is New Year's Day 2027? | Friday | Saturday | Thursday | Sunday
exercise: Halloween 2026 is a Saturday. What day is Bonfire Night, 5 days later? | Thursday | Wednesday | Friday | Saturday
exercise: What does Bonfire Night remember? | A plot in 1605 to blow up Parliament | The end of the First World War in 1918 | The first fireworks ever made in China | The day King James the First was crowned
exercise: The 1st of the month is a Tuesday. What day is the 15th? | Tuesday | Wednesday | Monday | Thursday
exercise: The 1st is a Tuesday. Which of these dates is also a Tuesday? | The 22nd | The 21st | The 14th | The 28th
exercise: Mia's sports day is "the second Friday in June". 1 June is a Monday. What date is it? | 12 June | 5 June | 9 June | 13 June
exercise: Max says, "My birthday's always on a Saturday!" Why can't that be true? | The weekday of a date moves on every year | Birthdays are never allowed on Saturdays | Saturdays move to a new month each year | The week has a different length each year
exercise: How many Friday the 13ths are there in 2026? | 3 | 1 | 12 | 0
exercise: Is Friday the 13th really unlucky? | No, it is just a superstition | Yes, accidents double on that day | Yes, but only in the leap years | No, Tuesday the 13th is the unlucky one
exercise: Ryan asks his phone what day 1 January 2000 was. What does it say? | Saturday | Monday | Friday | Sunday
exercise: A 30-day month starts on a Thursday. Payday is the last Friday. What date is that? | The 30th | The 29th | The 27th | The 23rd
exercise: What trick did John Conway invent? | The Doomsday rule for finding the weekday of any date | The knuckle trick for months | The rule for leap years | The 24-hour clock
test: Kai counts on from Monday: "10 days, so Wednesday next week." What's right? | Thursday; 10 days is a week and 3 days | Wednesday; he counted right | Friday; 10 days is a week and 4 | Monday; 10 days brings the same day
test: Harry: "Christmas is a Friday, so New Year's Day's Friday too, no cap." Is he right? | Yes, they are exactly 7 days apart | No, New Year's Day is on a Saturday | No, New Year's Day is on a Thursday | No, those two days never share a weekday
test: Max: "My birthday's always on a Saturday!" His sister: "No chance." Who's right? | The sister; birthdays move round the week | Max; birthdays always keep the same weekday | Max, but only in leap years | Neither; birthdays are always on Sundays
test: Emily's aunt says Friday the 13th is unlucky and checks 2026: three of them. What should Emily say? | It's a superstition; nothing special happens | Then 2026 will be three times as unlucky | Friday the 13th happens only every 3 years | Every month has a Friday the 13th
test: A Delhi cousin: "Sir has preponed the party by exactly 7 days, it was on Sunday." What day is the new party? | Sunday, a week earlier | Saturday, a week earlier | Sunday, a whole week later | Monday, eight days earlier
test: Lily's teacher: "1st of the month's a Tuesday, what's the 15th, y'all?" A boy shouts, "Thursday, cos 15 is odd!" Put him right. | Tuesday; 15 is 14 days, two whole weeks, after the 1st | Thursday; odd dates fall on Thursdays | Wednesday; add one day each week | Monday; the 15th always is
test: What would happen to the weekdays if the week had 8 days instead of 7? | The same day would come back every 8 days instead of 7 | Every month would have exactly 4 weeks | Christmas would always be on a Sunday | Nothing would change at all
test: Zoe's mum: "Payday's the last Friday, month's 30 days, starts on a Thursday. Do the needful and tell me the date." | The 30th | The 29th | The 2nd | The 23rd
test: Mia, Gen Alpha (today's kids) and extra: "Sports day's the second Friday, June 1st is Monday, so it's June 2nd, it's giving Friday." Put her right. | It is 12 June; the first Friday is 5 June | It is 2 June, the second day | It is 5 June, the first Friday | It is 8 June, the second Monday
test: Ryan: "1 January 2000 was a Saturday? You're having a laugh, how would the phone know?" | Calendar rules let computers work out any date's weekday | Someone typed in every date by hand | Phones guess the day at random | Phones only know dates after 2010
test: In a cartoon, Halloween is a Saturday and Bonfire Night five days later is "also a Saturday". Put it right. | It is a Thursday | It is a Wednesday | It is a Friday too | It is still a Saturday
exam: It is given that the present day is Monday. Determine the day of the week upon which an event ten days hence shall occur. | Thursday | Wednesday | Friday | Monday
exam: Whereas the first day of a month falls upon a Tuesday, ascertain the day of the week of the fifteenth. | Tuesday | Wednesday | Monday | Thursday
exam: Identify the date of "the second Friday in June", given that the first of June is a Monday. | 12 June | 5 June | 9 June | 13 June
exam: Select the response that is consistent with the established facts concerning the weekday of a fixed date in successive ordinary years. | It advances by one day each year | It remains unchanged every single year | It advances by seven days each year | It recedes by one day each and every year
